{#
  The shell every page extends.

  Two things here are the whole reason lava/view exists rather than a bare Twig
  install, and both are visible from this file:

   - `url('home')` and `url('tasks.index')` take a route NAME. A hardcoded
     `/tasks` in a template means renaming the route silently breaks every link
     and nothing warns — the route still matches, the page still renders, and
     the link 404s. Going through the router means a bad link is impossible: an
     unknown name is an `unknown_route` problem naming the route.

   - `feature('tasks_csv_export')` answers whether a flag is on, from the same
     resolver the router uses to decide whether the route exists at all. So the
     link and the route disappear together — the template cannot advertise a
     page the router would 404, and `LAVA_FEATURE_TASKS_CSV_EXPORT=off` turns
     both off without touching either file.

  Escaping is not configured here because it is not configurable: the pack sets
  `autoescape` to html always, so every `{{ … }}` below is escaped whether the
  file is named `.twig` or `.html.twig`. The dangerous spelling is the one you
  have to type — `{{ value|raw }}`.
#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{% block title %}LavaPHP demo{% endblock %}</title>
  <style>
    :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
    body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem; }
    header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; align-items: baseline; border-bottom: 1px solid #8884; padding-bottom: .75rem; }
    header a { text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
    nav { display: flex; gap: 1rem; font-size: .875rem; font-weight: 400; }
    table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem; }
    th, td { text-align: left; padding: .4rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #8884; }
    td.done { text-decoration: line-through; opacity: .6; }
    .muted { color: #888; font-size: .875rem; }
    footer { margin-top: 2.5rem; border-top: 1px solid #8884; padding-top: .75rem; }
    code { font-size: .875em; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <a href="{{ url('home') }}">Tasks</a>
    <nav>
      <a href="{{ url('tasks.index') }}">/tasks (JSON)</a>
      {% if feature('tasks_csv_export') %}
        <a href="{{ url('tasks.export') }}">/tasks/export (CSV)</a>
      {% endif %}
      <a href="{{ url('upstream.health') }}">/upstream/health</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>{% block content %}{% endblock %}</main>

  <footer class="muted">
    Rendered by <code>lava/view</code>; every value on this page is escaped.
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
